		{
			"name": "Load Testing",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Rate Limit Test (Rapid Fire)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"// This test should eventually hit rate limit",
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 202 or 429\", function () {",
									"    pm.expect([202, 429]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
									"});",
									"",
									"// Check for Retry-After header on 429",
									"if (pm.response.code === 429) {",
									"    pm.test(\"Retry-After header present\", function () {",
									"        pm.response.to.have.header(\"Retry-After\");",
									"    });",
									"}"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						},
						{
							"listen": "prerequest",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"// Use same user_id to trigger per-user rate limit",
									"pm.environment.set(\"user_id\", \"rate_limit_test_user\");"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n    \"user_id\": \"{{user_id}}\",\n    \"merchant_id\": \"merchant_load_test\",\n    \"amount\": 1000,\n    \"currency\": \"USD\",\n    \"method\": \"CREDIT_CARD\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/payments",
							"host": [
								"{{base_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"v1",
								"payments"
							]
						},
						"description": "Run this request in Postman Runner with high iterations to test rate limiting.\n\n**Expected Behavior:**\n- First ~100 requests: 202 Accepted\n- After rate limit: 429 Too Many Requests\n- Retry-After header indicates wait time\n\n**Rate Limit Configuration:**\n- 100 requests per second per user\n- Burst capacity: 200 requests\n\n**How to Test:**\n1. Open Runner in Postman\n2. Set iterations: 300\n3. Set delay: 0ms\n4. Run and observe rate limit in action"
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Backpressure Test (System Overload)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"// When system is overloaded, expect 503",
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 202 or 503\", function () {",
									"    pm.expect([202, 503]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
									"});",
									"",
									"// Check for Retry-After on backpressure",
									"if (pm.response.code === 503) {",
									"    pm.test(\"Backpressure applied - Retry-After header present\", function () {",
									"        pm.response.to.have.header(\"Retry-After\");",
									"    });",
									"}"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						},
						{
							"listen": "prerequest",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"pm.environment.set(\"user_id\", \"user_\" + Date.now() + \"_\" + Math.random());"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n    \"user_id\": \"{{user_id}}\",\n    \"merchant_id\": \"merchant_stress\",\n    \"amount\": 5000,\n    \"currency\": \"USD\",\n    \"method\": \"CREDIT_CARD\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/payments",
							"host": [
								"{{base_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"v1",
								"payments"
							]
						},
						"description": "Test system backpressure when worker pool queue is full.\n\n**Expected Behavior:**\n- When worker pool queue < 90% full: 202 Accepted\n- When worker pool queue ≥ 90% full: 503 Service Unavailable\n\n**Configuration:**\n- Worker pool size: 50 workers\n- Queue capacity: 1,000 tasks\n- Backpressure threshold: 900 tasks (90%)\n\n**How to Test:**\n1. Run with high concurrency in Runner\n2. Set iterations: 2000+\n3. Delay: 0ms\n4. Monitor for 503 responses (backpressure in action)"
					},
					"response": []
				}
			],
			"description": "Load testing and stress testing scenarios.\n\n**Note:** Use Postman Runner or Newman for automated load testing.\n\n**Example Newman command:**\n```bash\nnewman run Payment-API.postman_collection.json \\\n  -e payment-api.postman_environment.json \\\n  -n 1000 \\\n  --delay-request 0\n```"
		},
